# Tool Registration

Whenever you define a new tool with `@rekog/mcp-nest` (a `@Tool({...})` decorated method in a `*.tool.ts` file), you must also register it in two places:

1. `src/modules/systemChats/systemChatTools.service.ts` — add an entry inside `buildTools()` so the tool is available in system chats. Import the Zod params schema from the `*.tool.ts` file and call the matching facade (never the service directly — see `architecture.mdc`).
2. `src/mcp.tag.ts` — add a row to the "Available tools" table in `mcpTagDescription` with the tool's kebab-case name and description.

Use the **kebab-case** tool name (e.g. `create-character`) in `mcp.tag.ts` and the **snake_case** key (e.g. `create_character`) in `systemChatTools.service.ts`, matching the existing entries.

## Example

After adding a new tool in `src/modules/characters/characters.tool.ts`:

```typescript
@Tool({
  name: 'archive-character',
  description: 'Archive a character so they no longer appear in the city',
  parameters: archiveCharacterParams,
  annotations: { readOnlyHint: false },
})
async archiveCharacter({ id }: { id: string }) { ... }
```

Add it to `systemChatTools.service.ts`:

```typescript
import { archiveCharacterParams } from '../characters/characters.tool';

archive_character: tool({
  description: 'Archive a character so they no longer appear in the city',
  inputSchema: archiveCharacterParams,
  execute: async ({ id }) => {
    await this.characterFacade.archive(id);
    return `Character ${id} archived`;
  },
}),
```

And add a row to `mcp.tag.ts`:

```typescript
| \`archive-character\` | Archive a character so they no longer appear in the city |
```
